   245	### 3.3 The order-0 GALOIS layer: the star congruence
   246	
   247	Moh's search condition **(8)** (moh.txt:3299 ff.) introduces exactly the object that does
   248	kill:
   249	
   250	> (8) … let the l.c.m. of the reduced denominators of `δ_s,…,δ_r` be `L`. Then `Δ_{r−1}` is
   251	> defined to be the reduced denominator of `L δ_{r−1}`. … Due to the existence of the
   252	> following automorphism … `t ↦ ω t` where `ω` is a `Δ_{r−1}`-th root of unity, the value of
   253	> `V_{r−1}` is further restricted by (10) … if the corresponding factor of `p(π)` is of the
   254	> form `π − α` with `α ≠ 0` or … (11) … if the corresponding factor of `p(π)` is of the
   255	> form `π`.
   256	
   257	> **THEOREM (10)₁ (PROVED-HERE; = Moh (8)–(11) at `r = 1`, sharpened by D1-STAR(d)).**
   258	> Let `L_1 := lcm{den δ_s, …, den δ_2}` and `Δ_1 :=` reduced denominator of `L_1 δ_1`. Then
   259	> ```text
   260	>          a_1 = e V_2  ≡  0  or  1   (mod Δ_1).
   261	> ```
   262	>
   263	> *Proof.* By Moh's search condition (4) the `δ_i` are the characteristic exponents of the
   264	> branch, so every exponent of `σ_1` has denominator dividing `L_1`, i.e.
   265	> `σ_1 ∈ K_1 := C((x^{-1/L_1}))`. Write `δ_1 = p/q` in lowest terms; then
   266	> `lcm(L_1,q) = L_1Δ_1` and `Gal(C((x^{-1/L_1Δ_1}))/K_1)` is cyclic of order `Δ_1`,
   267	> generated by `τ : T ↦ ζT` with `T = x^{-1/(L_1Δ_1)}` and `ζ` primitive. `τ` fixes `σ_1`
   268	> and sends `x^{-δ_1} ↦ ζ^{L_1Δ_1δ_1} x^{-δ_1}` with `gcd(L_1Δ_1δ_1, Δ_1) = 1`, so `τ`
   269	> multiplies the leading coefficient `ξ` of `ρ − σ_1` by a **primitive** `Δ_1`-th root of
   270	> unity. `τ` permutes the roots of `g` and preserves `D_1`, so the set `{ξ_1,…,ξ_{a_1}}`
   271	> — which by TF-0 has `a_1` **distinct** elements — is stable under that multiplication.
   272	> Its orbits have size `Δ_1` except the orbit `{0}`, which occurs at most once. ∎
