   288	### 3.4 Order `ν > 0`: the operator, in closed form
   289	
   290	Substituting `Φ_ν = Qφ`, `Γ_ν = Pψ` and setting `X := dψ − eφ`, `Y := φ + ψ`,
   291	`ν̂ := ν/(1−δ_1)`, one gets the compact form
   292	
   293	```text
   294	      L_ν(Qφ, Pψ)  =  γ (1 − ν̂) Y  +  κ [ ν̂ (PQ)' X  +  PQ X' ] .
   295	```
   296	
   297	For the `V = 1` bottom form (`P = π³+3π`, `Q = π²+2`, `d,e = 2,3`) the matrix of `L̃_ν̃` on
   298	`{deg F ≤ 3} × {deg G ≤ 4}` is `6 × 9` of generic rank 6 (`kernel_L.py`, `tfcal.py`):
   299	
   300	```text
   301	   ν̃        1/7  1/3   1    2    3    4    5   11/2   7
   302	   nullity    3    3    4    4    3    3    3    3    3
   303	```
   304	
   305	The three generic kernel vectors are identified: `(F,G) = (−Q', −P')` is the shift
   306	`y ↦ y + a x^{-δ_1-ν}` of the whole chart (a gauge move, not geometry); the rank drop at
   307	`ν̃ = d = 2` is `f ↦ f + const`, at `ν̃ = e = 3` it is `g ↦ g + const`. So the first
   308	correction order is **positive-dimensional** and does not kill by itself.
   309	
   310	**Which `Φ_ν, Γ_ν` are geometrically realisable?** From the product structure
   311	`Γ = Π_g(x)·∏_{k}(π − ξ_k − u_k(x))·∏_{j∉D_1}(1 + π w_j)`,
   312	
   313	```text
   314	   Γ_ν = P(π)·(c_0 + c_1 π + c_2 π² + …) − Σ_k u_{k,ν} P/(π−ξ_k),
   315	   Φ_ν = Q(π)·(b_0 + b_1 π + …)        − Σ_j v_{j,ν} Q/(π−η_j),
   316	```
   317	
   318	and since `{P/(π−ξ_k)}` is a Lagrange basis of `C[π]_{≤a_1−1}`, the realisable space at the
   319	first order is **all** of `C[π]_{≤b_1+1} × C[π]_{≤a_1+1}`. Hence the 3-dimensional kernel is
   320	the honest answer at order `ε`: **positive-dimensional, dimension 3**.
   321	
   322	### 3.5 The NO-TAME theorem, and `h'(C) = 0`
   323	
   324	The picture changes if the star's own tails are silent at that order.
   325	
   326	> **THEOREM TF-NOTAME (PROVED-HERE; machine-checked at `V = 1`).** Suppose at order `ν` the
   327	> tame tails contribute nothing, i.e. `Γ_ν = P(g_0 + g_1π)` and `Φ_ν = Q(f_0 + f_1π)`. Then
   328	> `L_ν = 0` forces `f_0 = f_1 = g_0 = g_1 = 0`, for every `ν ≠ 1 − δ_1`.
   329	>
   330	> *Proof.* The `π^{(d+e)V}` coefficient gives `dg_1 = ef_1`; the `π^{(d+e)V−1}` one gives
   331	> `dg_0 = ef_0`; substituting, `L_ν = πγ s[(d+e) − ν/κ] + γσ[(d+e) − ν/κ]` with
   332	> `f_1 = ds, g_1 = es, f_0 = dσ, g_0 = eσ`, and `(d+e) − ν/κ = 0` exactly at `ν = 1−δ_1`. ∎
   333	> At `ν = 1−δ_1` (`ν̃ = d+e = 5`) the driver returns the residual family `g_i = (e/d) f_i`.
   334	
   335	The geometric meaning of `g_1` and `f_1` is explicit. At level 2, Moh Prop 4.6(1) gives
   336	`g_σ = p_2^{n/d_2} = p_2^{e}` and `T^ψ_{1,σ} = p_2^{m/d_2} = p_2^{d}`, and the bottom disc is
   337	a root `C` of `p_2` of multiplicity `V_2`. Writing `h := p_2/(π−C)^{V_2}`, the outer roots
   338	nearest `D_1` sit at contact `δ_2`, so at `ν = ε := δ_1 − δ_2`
   339	
   340	```text
   341	      g_1 = e·h'(C)/h(C),      f_1 = d·h'(C)/h(C)     (ratio d : e automatic).
   342	```
   343	
   344	So under the NO-TAME hypothesis at `ν = ε`,
   345	
   346	```text
   347	      (TF-1)      h'(C) = 0,   i.e.   Σ_{j ≠ i} V_j/(C_i − C_j)  +  w'(C_i)/w(C_i) = 0
   348	```
   349	
   350	for every bottom-major disc `C_i`, where `p_2 = ∏_i (π−C_i)^{V_i} · w(π)`.
