   352	### 3.6 The exhausting corollary
   353	
   354	> **COROLLARY TF-EXH (PROVED-HERE; identity machine-checked, `k = 2..6`).** If the
   355	> bottom-major discs exhaust their `D_2` (`w` constant; for `s = 3` this is
   356	> `Σ_B V_2(B) = u = deg p_2`, i.e. the ceiling `N = U` attained), then under the NO-TAME
   357	> hypothesis there is **at most one** bottom-major disc.
