  3594	                                Appendix II. Some special cases
  3595	
  3596	      A simple Computer program shows that the only possible counter-examples to the
  3597	Jacobian conjecture for polynomials of degrees less than 100 are of degrees (64, 68),
  3598	(84, 56), (75, 50) and (99, 66) with some special data attached. A routine computation
  3599	shows that the numbers of coefficients of the pairs of polynomials involved are 3370,
  3600	5308, 4352 and 7348 respectively. The task of direct verification of the Jacobian con-
  3601	jecture by computation for those pairs of polynomials with the said degrees is beyond
  3602	the capacity of a large Computer. In this Appendix we shall illustrate some methods to
  3603	reduce the numbers of coefficients, and then settle the problems of computations.
