codex
The scan changes the calibration: Moh’s printed (10) uses his quotient from division by the denominator increment, while the charged report renamed the denominator increment as Δ. Also, p.201 prints separate final `r = 2` divisibility alternatives (12)-(13), so the proposed `(10)_1` is a derived necessary condition, not literally Moh’s printed bottom condition.
codex
I’m widening the code read to the helper drivers named in the charge. The key question is not just whether a condition appears in comments, but whether any branch rejects on it.
