     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""
     3	D1-SUBTREE -- part B: the floor on N from the bottom of Moh's tower.
     4	
     5	Inputs re-derived here, not imported as claims:
     6	  Moh Lemma 5.2 (p.178, verbatim):  ((n-L)/d_r) lambda* = -1 + delta*,  hence at the
     7	     general point of D_r,   lambda_g(delta_r) = ord_t g(sigma_r) = n(delta_r-1)/(n-M_r).
     8	  Moh Def 5.1(1) (p.179, verbatim): D_i holds (n/d_{i+1})V_{i+1} roots of g and
     9	     (-mu_j/d_{i+1})V_{i+1} roots of T_j^psi;  with -mu_1 = m this gives
    10	     lambda_f(delta_r) = (m/n) lambda_g(delta_r).
    11	  Moh Prop 6.1(1) (p.190-191, verbatim, r >= 2): on a minor branch, delta < 1 implies
    12	     ord g(sigma) < 0, i.e. the g-frontier there has delta^0 >= 1.
    13	
    14	THEOREM D1-PIN (this lane).  Put L_r := 1 - delta_r.  For a root rho of g in a
    15	bottom-major disc D_1, with contribution c_rho = (-lambda_f(delta^0_rho))^+ to N:
    16	    FLOOR    c_rho = 1 - delta^0_rho  >=  L_1 + lambda_g(delta_1) = L_1 m/(n+m)
    17	             [JAC-FIBRE + lambda_g has slope >= 1 below delta_1]
    18	    CEILING  c_rho = -lambda_f(delta^0_rho) <= -lambda_f(delta_1) = L_1 m/(n+m)
    19	             [lambda_f nondecreasing + Def 5.1(1)]
    20	  The two coincide -- and, as verified below, coincide at r = 1 and at NO other level,
    21	  because -M_1 = m is exactly the leading exponent of f.  Hence c_rho is PINNED and
    22	    N  =  sum over bottom-major discs B of  a(B) (1-delta_1(B)) d/(d+e)
